  "_doc": "ADR-0028 D4 pre-registered host behavior contract registry. Consumed by tests only; hooks never read it at runtime (R4). exit_codes are the hook PROCESS exit codes observed by tests, asserted with config env (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR pointing at a fixture dir); how a host INTERPRETS those exit codes is a host-side semantic recorded in note (R6), not shimmed (audit 2026-08-29: clarified after copilot note ambiguity). Entry fields: {id, host, event, exit_codes, decision_keys, decision_values, fail_soft, term, source_adr, transcript_file}. Executable entries add hook (single script) or hooks (script list), spawned by test/host-contracts.test.js with fixture stdin. Config entries add config + expect_events. Instruction entries add files. Optional note field records known degradations honestly (R6). term must anchor a CONTEXT.md glossary term (existence anchor, not prose parsing). lifecycle: per-adapter state (active|deprecated|eol); retirement triggers: official shutdown announcement, repository archival, or consecutive protocol-breaking versions without docs (ADR-0028 D6). Change governance: editing this file requires a docs/adr/*.md or CONTEXT.md change in the same commit range (scripts/check-host-contracts.js reuses the ADR-0027 coupling rule). transcript_file (ADR-0070 D-C(c)) records per-host conviction-lane reachability: present = the host is documented to deliver transcript_path on the stop-family event (claude-code); absent = the host has no stop-family hook channel at all (instruction-tier hosts); unverifiable = the event exists but transcript delivery is not documented.",
